INT. CURLING CLUB LOUNGE, SECOND-FLOOR VIEWING GLASS - EVENING

The rink below glows blue-white. Granite stones glide silently across ice. A scoreboard reads END 9 / TIED 4-4. The lounge is a warm cave of wood paneling, trophies, and a single fan whirring pointlessly.

HADLEY BRANTFORD (40s, team skip, wool sweater, thermos of something stronger than tea) leans on the railing. Behind her, on a leather couch, her teammates ABDULLAH FARRUKH (30s, sweeper, ice-burned cheeks) and WINIFRED "WINNIE" SOLBERG (20s, rookie, ponytail, quivering) sit with their brooms across their laps. At the bar, a retired champion, ARCHIBALD "ARCHIE" TWOMBLY (70s, cardigan, commentator headset around his neck), polishes a glass.

HADLEY
Winnie, your delivery.

WINNIE
I know.

HADLEY
You pulled it left in the eighth.

WINNIE
I know.

HADLEY
It's all right to know. I'd just like you to fix it.

ABDULLAH
She's got it, Hadley.

HADLEY
Does she?

WINNIE
I've got it.

HADLEY
Then say it with your whole face.

WINNIE
(breathing in)
I have got it.

HADLEY
Better.

ARCHIE
(from the bar)
Back in '71, I threw the last stone with a broken wrist.

ABDULLAH
We know, Archie.

ARCHIE
Won, too.

HADLEY
(to the room)
Everyone's very proud of Archie.

A bell rings below. The teams are called to the ice. Winnie rises first. Abdullah follows, and Hadley screws the cap onto her thermos.

ARCHIE
(into his headset)
This is Archie Twombly, live from the Glenmore Club. The last end is about to begin.

Hadley, muttering to herself, does not turn around.

HADLEY
(muttering)
Don't blow it, Brantford.

A phone buzzes on the bar. Archie answers.

DISPATCH (V.O.)
(over phone)
Archie? It's the broadcast truck. We've lost your feed. Is the skip ready?

ARCHIE
(into phone)
She's ready. They're all ready.

Hadley stops at the stairs. She looks down at the ice, pale and shining.

HADLEY
(quietly)
Winnie. Whatever happens, you throw the last one.

WINNIE
Me? Hadley, no.

HADLEY
You. It's what you were born for.

ABDULLAH
(low, to Winnie)
She's right.

WINNIE
Okay. Okay.

They file down the stairs. Archie watches through the glass as three small figures step onto the ice.

DISPATCH (V.O.)
(over phone)
Archie, we're back. Go ahead.

ARCHIE
(into headset)
And here they come.

He lifts a glass to the window and sets it down untouched.
